'''Pémono''' is a [[Cariban language]] or dialect of [[Mapoyo language]] that was spoken by only an eighty-year-old woman when discovered in 1998 in [[Venezuela]]. The ethnic population now speaks Spanish. It became extinct some time after that.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last=Mattei-Muller |first=Marie-Claude |date=2003 |title=Pémono: eslabón perdido entre mapoyo y yawarana: lenguas caribes ergativas de la Guayana noroccidental de Venezuela |url=https://amerindia.cnrs.fr/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Pe%CC%81mono-eslabo%CC%81n-perdido-entre-mapoyo-y-yawarana-lenguas-caribes-ergativas-de-la-Guayana-noroccidental-de-Venezuela.-Marie-Claude-MATTEI-MULLER.pdf |journal=Amérindia: revue d'ethnolinguistique amérindienne |volume=28 |pages=33–54}}</ref>

